local _, HT = ...
HT.Guide = {
    {"Read the route", "Each large number is a map stop. Inside it, 1.1, 1.2 and so on are separate substeps. The action label says PICK UP, COMPLETE OBJECTIVE, or TURN IN. Needed by names only the players who still need that task. Nearby tasks share one stop."},
    {"Follow the direction arrow", "The tracker points directly to the next stop and shows yards. Turn your character until the arrow points up. At the stop means you are nearby, not that the quest is complete. The arrow does not find roads or avoid obstacles. It pauses when position or map scale is unavailable."},
    {"Travel time and party positions", "The GPS estimates straight-line travel time using your current movement speed, or walking speed when stopped. Terrain, roads, combat, and mounts can change the real trip. Party members running this addon share their current map position within the party. Blue map pins and the party panel show recent positions; they disappear when data gets old."},
    {"Quest chains and level gaps", "If a stronger shared quest appears one or two prerequisite quests or levels away, Details shows a potential unlock and who needs each step. A missing chain step can come from another zone. These are suggestions until the game confirms the quest is available; current confirmed stops remain your active route."},
    {"Solo or demo?", "SOLO MODE uses your real character and quests. PARTY MODE uses your party. DEMO · SIMULATED uses fictional quests; click Exit demo or type /plx live to return to your character. Being alone never starts the demo automatically."},
    {"On-screen tracker", "Close Details to follow your route on the small tracker. Drag it to move it. /plx hud toggles it; /plx hud show restores it. The tracker lists the current stop, who needs it, and upcoming stops. Use Previous or Skip / Next to change the GPS target without completing a quest. Popout GPS detaches the arrow; drag it, then use Dock GPS to return it. In the solo preview, Next step advances the simulated route."},
    {"1. Try it solo", "Type /plx demo or click Try solo demo. Three sample players show how shared quests and XP differences affect the route. Questie is not needed for this preview."},
    {"2. Follow the gold stop", "Start with the highlighted NEXT card. Its number matches the route overview and, in live mode, the world map. Nearby tasks share one stop. The For line names who needs each task."},
    {"3. Practice the full route", "In demo mode, Next step completes the highlighted simulated stop. Pickups become objectives, then turn-ins. Reset demo starts over. Exit demo returns to your character. Nothing in the demo changes your quests."},
    {"4. Quest with friends", "For live routes, every Horde party member needs PlxTogether and a Forever-compatible Questie. Form a normal party and meet in the same zone. Wait for everyone to show Ready. Missing or stale data pauses shared recommendations."},
    {"5. Complete quests normally", "Pick up, complete, and turn in quests yourself. The route updates as progress arrives. World map opens numbered stops. The overview is a schematic, not a road map. Refresh route reorders from your current position."},
    {"6. Understand the XP", "Why these quests? shows each member's estimated quest XP and level retention. A lower retention means a level penalty. The planner favors quests everyone can do and gives extra weight to the lowest individual benefit. XP estimates still need Forever beta validation."},
    {"7. If no route appears", "Check the party summary, then /plx status. Confirm everyone uses the same addon version and zone, Questie has loaded, and you are not in a raid. Some quests may be completed, locked, missing XP, or have no local coordinates. Use /reload if an addon has just been updated."},
    {"Commands", "/plx — window\n/plx guide — this guide\n/plx demo — solo preview\n/plx demo next — advance preview\n/plx demo reset — restart preview\n/plx live — leave preview\n/plx refresh — refresh route\n/plx map — world map\n/plx status — party readiness\n/plx list — print recommendations"},
}
